# Parental Controls: allow the service user to lock/unlock accounts and
# manage user sessions. Scoped to exact binaries; usernames are validated
# by the app ([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+, must exist in /etc/passwd).
# Install as /etc/sudoers.d/parental-controls (mode 0440) and check
# with `visudo -c`.
#
# Both /usr/sbin and /usr/bin are listed because the app invokes bare names
# (`sudo usermod`, `sudo loginctl`, `sudo passwd`) and sudo resolves them via
# secure_path (sbin first). The pairs are hardlinks to the same files, but
# sudo matches on the path string, so only the resolved path authorizes.
# `passwd` is scoped to `-S` (read-only status check) — never password changes.
#
# `systemd-run` exists for the notification path only. notify_user() runs
#   systemd-run --machine=<user>@.host --user notify-send -u critical <t> <b>
# so pre-lock warnings reach the child's own session. The machine transport
# talks to the *system* bus, which polkit refuses for the unprivileged service
# user ("Failed to connect to system scope bus via machine transport:
# Permission denied"), so the call has to arrive through sudo. Root is the only
# runas that can open it. Only notify-send is authorized as the payload: sudoers
# matches arguments as one concatenated string, so a bare `--user *` would also
# authorize any other command in a child's session (sudoers(5), "Preventing
# shell escapes").
#
# NOTE: sudoers authorizes the `systemd-run ...` command, not sudo itself, so
# this rule applies when the service reaches it through sudo — the form every
# other privileged call in the app uses.
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/usermod -L *, /usr/bin/usermod -L *, /usr/sbin/usermod -U *, /usr/bin/usermod -U *
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/loginctl terminate-user *, /usr/bin/loginctl terminate-user *
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/loginctl show-user *, /usr/bin/loginctl show-user *, /usr/sbin/loginctl lock-session *, /usr/bin/loginctl lock-session *
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/loginctl show-session *, /usr/bin/loginctl show-session *
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/passwd -S *, /usr/bin/passwd -S *
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/systemd-run --machine=*@.host --user notify-send -u critical * *, /usr/bin/systemd-run --machine=*@.host --user notify-send -u critical * *
